# PDF to Text Conversion

## src/transfert_pdf_txt.py

- Converts PDF files to text format
- Uses pytesseract and OpenCV for OCR
- Implements column detection for better text extraction
- Preserves document structure in the output text
- Replaces original PDFs with text versions after conversion

### Key Functions

#### detect_columns()

```python
def detect_columns(image):
    """Détecte automatiquement les colonnes en analysant la distribution du texte."""
```

- Analyzes text distribution in the image
- Uses Tesseract OCR to extract text positions
- Creates histograms of text distribution
- Identifies column boundaries using peak detection
- Returns structured text blocks organized by columns

#### convert_and_replace_pdfs()

```python
def convert_and_replace_pdfs(folder_path):
    """Converts PDFs to text files and replaces the originals."""
```

- Processes all PDF files in the specified directory
- Converts each page to images using pdf2image
- Detects columns in each page
- Writes structured text to output files
- Removes original PDF files after successful conversion

### Implementation Notes

- Preserves page and column structure in output text
- Uses intelligent column detection for multi-column documents
- Handles OCR with pytesseract
- Image processing with OpenCV and numpy
